== Validating Fits With Cobalt Shifts

We determine the optimal Cobalt shift by marginalizing over the individual shift fits. To avoid bias from a potential signal, we exclude the $0 nu beta beta$ peak region (2515-2540 keV, \~95% $0 nu beta beta$ coverage) during this selection, effectively "blinding" the marginalization process to the true decay rate.

While we use the blinded fits to select the best-fit cobalt shift, the final posterior is the weighted sum of the posteriors from each shift, as detailed in the next section.

